### Network Inventory Sync — request collection
### Compatible with REST Client (VS Code) and the IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Requires the server running: npm start

@host = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@storeA = sk_store_a_demo
@storeB = sk_store_b_demo
@storeC = sk_store_c_demo
@admin = sk_admin_demo


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1 · Health and catalog
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Health (public, no API key)
GET {{host}}/health

### Stores
GET {{host}}/stores
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Products with their thresholds
GET {{host}}/products
X-API-Key: {{admin}}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2 · Reporting movements
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Sale at store-a -> 201, stock drops by exactly 3
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{storeA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "BOOK-HB-WK",
  "type": "OUT",
  "quantity": 3,
  "reason": "pos-sale"
}

### Warehouse receipt at store-b -> 201
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{storeB}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "BOOK-HB-WK",
  "type": "IN",
  "quantity": 25,
  "reason": "warehouse-receipt"
}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3 · The two cases that define the design
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3.1 OVERSELLING — ask for more than what's available.
### Returns 409 INSUFFICIENT_STOCK with the units on hand.
### The guard lives in the UPDATE, so there is no window between read and write.
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{storeA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "BOOK-HB-WK",
  "type": "OUT",
  "quantity": 99999
}

### 3.2 ISOLATION — store-a trying to report for store-b.
### Returns 403 STORE_MISMATCH: store_id is derived from the API key.
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{storeA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "store_id": "store-b",
  "sku": "BOOK-HB-WK",
  "type": "OUT",
  "quantity": 1
}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4 · Validation and authentication
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### No API key -> 401
GET {{host}}/inventory

### The admin key cannot write -> 403 STORE_KEY_REQUIRED
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "BOOK-CSP-CAPTIVE", "type": "IN", "quantity": 1 }

### Unknown field and invalid quantity -> 400 with per-field detail
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{storeA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "BOOK-CSP-CAPTIVE", "type": "IN", "qty": -3 }

### Product not in the catalog -> 404
POST {{host}}/movements
X-API-Key: {{storeA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "DOES-NOT-EXIST", "type": "IN", "quantity": 1 }


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5 · Queries
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Network-wide consolidated inventory
GET {{host}}/inventory
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Only products under their threshold
GET {{host}}/inventory?low_stock=true
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Per-store breakdown
GET {{host}}/inventory?group_by=store&store_id=store-a
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Stock range and category
GET {{host}}/inventory?category=fantasy&min_qty=10&max_qty=60
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Product detail: breakdown, open alert, and recent movements
GET {{host}}/inventory/BOOK-HB-WK
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### History filtered by product and type
GET {{host}}/movements?sku=BOOK-HB-WK&type=OUT&page_size=10
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Recent activity across the network
GET {{host}}/activity?limit=15
X-API-Key: {{admin}}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 6 · Alerts and thresholds
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Open alerts
GET {{host}}/alerts
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### History of resolved alerts
GET {{host}}/alerts?status=RESOLVED
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Raise the threshold above the current stock.
### Re-evaluates immediately: the response carries the OPENED event.
PATCH {{host}}/products/BOOK-HB-WK/threshold
X-API-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "low_stock_threshold": 500 }

### Lower it again: the response carries the RESOLVED event.
PATCH {{host}}/products/BOOK-HB-WK/threshold
X-API-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "low_stock_threshold": 12 }

### No admin key -> 403
PATCH {{host}}/products/BOOK-HB-WK/threshold
X-API-Key: {{storeA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "low_stock_threshold": 5 }


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 7 · Consistency check
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Compares the projection against the sum of the ledger.
### Must always return { "consistent": true, "discrepancies": [] },
### even with the simulator running in parallel.
GET {{host}}/reconcile
X-API-Key: {{admin}}
